     The idea of screen size is inherently interface dependent.
(A windowing interface could tell nethack an arbitrary size and
then use its own scrolling mechanisms without the core of nethack
knowing.)  For the tty interface, nethack keeps that information
in the variables LI and CO (which are macros used as shortcuts
for fields in tc_gbl_data) holding number of lines and columns.
Those macros and their underlying structure are defined for all
interfaces, but non-tty ones might not bother setting them to
nonzero.  And even tty might not have them set up yet at the
time of initial options processing, since one possible option is
window_type to select the interface.  This may be a case of "you
can't get there from here...".


